From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:30:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: don't warn on a brightness change left pending
 while the panel is off

The consumer blanks the panel before the DCP suspends. A brightness
change requested while the CRTC is off is not presented: the backlight
worker leaves it dirty and the enable swap on resume restores it. The
suspend drain treated that still-dirty change as a stuck present and,
after four drain passes, logged "brightness change still pending at
suspend" although the level was deferred by design and need not reach
the firmware before the mailbox suspends.

Return from the drain once a pending change remains only because the
panel is not lit. A change left pending while the panel is lit still
drains and warns as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
(cherry picked from commit 629e81bc2dd68f282e37c5a12d9bbd2b739d2098)
[k114s: aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1887 (merged 2026-11-14). Not booted on a K114s]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c           | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 2c0dd80547..95d69b1968 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -7201,6 +7201,16 @@ static void dcp_drain_for_sleep(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 			return;
 		if (!dcp_backlight_active(dcp) || !dcp_backlight_pending(dcp))
 			return;
+		/*
+		 * The consumer blanks the panel before this runs, so a change
+		 * left pending while the panel is not lit is the blank itself,
+		 * or a level set while DPMS was off: the firmware will not take
+		 * it until the CRTC is active again, and resume restores it on
+		 * the enable swap. It need not reach the firmware before the
+		 * mailbox suspends, so stop here rather than wait it out.
+		 */
+		if (!dcp_backlight_lit(dcp))
+			return;
 	}
 	dev_warn(dcp->dev, "brightness change still pending at suspend\n");
 }
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
index 46c162f201..80b9a52f57 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
@@ -462,6 +462,20 @@ bool dcp_backlight_pending(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	return pending;
 }
 
+/* The panel is showing a level now, so a pending change can be presented. */
+bool dcp_backlight_lit(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	bool lit;
+
+	if (!dcp_backlight_active(dcp))
+		return false;
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&dcp->backlight.lock, flags);
+	lit = dcp_bl_lit(&dcp->backlight.state);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dcp->backlight.lock, flags);
+	return lit;
+}
+
 /*
  * Called from the receive path, which must not queue a transaction itself;
  * the caller schedules the update worker when this returns true.  Requests
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
index cc2d321fb1..a746dfc29c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
@@ -395,6 +395,7 @@ int dcp_backlight_prepare(struct apple_dcp *dcp, bool have_surface,
 			  struct dcp_backlight_present *present);
 bool dcp_backlight_complete(struct apple_dcp *dcp, u64 sequence, bool accepted);
 bool dcp_backlight_pending(struct apple_dcp *dcp);
+bool dcp_backlight_lit(struct apple_dcp *dcp);
 bool dcp_backlight_resend(struct apple_dcp *dcp);
 unsigned int dcp_backlight_retry_delay(struct apple_dcp *dcp);
 
